{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779656418,"nonce":"8BtSHNIAVQGEocWaaWVVDWh5i/c=","title":"Teach auth flows the protected branch checkout path","message":"## Problem\n\nSome repos can have a protected integration branch that is not checked out at the repo root. Feedbax currently has root on main and develop in worktrees/develop, which has repeatedly caused agents and auth flows to inspect or operate from the wrong checkout. We are considering migrating Feedbax so the protected branch is checked out at the repo root, with main/release in a named worktree instead.\n\nMandible should be reviewed so auth request submission/merge, protected-branch detection, and any future repo provisioning are explicit about the protected branch checkout path rather than assuming either repo root or feature-worktree cwd.\n\n## Desired direction\n\n- Model or infer the protected branch checkout path consistently for auth requests.\n- Run protected-branch merge/auth operations from that checkout, or require an explicit target/cwd when layout is non-standard.\n- If Mandible eventually clones or provisions repos, default to checking out the protected integration branch at repo root and creating named worktrees for release/default branches when needed.\n- Keep dirty-worktree policy separate from checkout-path policy; dirty state is tracked by issue 350817b.\n\n## Acceptance notes\n\nReview current auth request code before changing Feedbax layout. If no Mandible code change is needed for the Feedbax migration, close this only with a comment explaining why the current auth code is layout-safe.","files":null}]}